cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite both the software (this record)
  and the associated publication.
title: >-
  Enabling Voices: LLM-assisted screening pipeline for a scoping review of
  AI-assisted communication support in dementia and aphasia
abstract: >-
  Code, prompts, and derived data for a scoping review of AI-assisted
  communication support for people with dementia and aphasia, and for its
  methodological contribution on locally hosted, open-source LLM-assisted
  screening. Includes the screening and extraction prompts, per-record model
  decisions with confidences and rationales, anonymised human annotations,
  record-level corpus metadata, and a script that regenerates every reported
  agreement and screening-performance statistic from the deposited records.
type: software
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/elisabethan2/EnablingVoices-deposit
keywords:
  - scoping review
  - large language models
  - AI-assisted screening
  - evidence synthesis
  - aphasia
  - dementia
  - reproducibility

